xcel tools (a colorful indicator recap with two charts, and a sheet listing the lowest indicators highlighted in red). Do not redesign, simplify, recolor, or rebrand the box. SET & PROPS: Puskesmas administration room in the morning: a gray filing cabinet with an open drawer of empty hanging folders, a desk with a laptop and a small potted plant, a wall calendar with blurred marks (no readable text), window daylight, no other people. TIMELINE — 10 seconds: 0–2s Hook · close-up: his hand pulls open a drawer of empty hanging folders; cut to medium shot as he turns to the camera. VO (ID, verbatim): "Saya baru pindah ke puskesmas ini." Delivery (EN): calm, honest 2–4s Problem · medium shot, he flips through the empty folders. VO (ID, verbatim): "Diminta menyusun PKP akhir tahun." Delivery (EN): serious 4–6s Problem · medium close-up, he closes the drawer slowly. VO (ID, verbatim): "File tahun lalu tidak ada." Delivery (EN): concerned 6–8s Problem · medium shot, he looks at the empty desk. VO (ID, verbatim): "Formatnya juga belum per klaster." Delivery (EN): firm 8–10s Beat · medium shot, he sits down and takes off his glasses for a moment. VO: none. AUDIO: Quiet office ambience, a metal drawer sliding, birds outside. Only the talent speaks. Natural Indonesian, conversational, clear pronunciation, no background music. Lighting/mood: realistic natural light matching the set, clean soft contrast, believable Indonesian setting, not glossy, not studio. Camera: follow the camera style above consistently; stable and restrained, no whip pans, no drone, no 360 orbit. Keep product readable whenever it is on screen. Performance: natural facial expression, believable professional UGC, natural eye contact, restrained gestures, no exaggerated acting. Lips clearly synced to each word. Hands: simple, natural, relaxed movements. CLEAN OUTPUT: No subtitles, captions, generated text overlays, watermark, poster layout, storyboard panels, or added graphics. Do not invent product details, claims, prices, ratings, testimonials, certifications, or guarantees. Keep exact talent face, the WARDROBE above, product shape, colors, packaging, box, printed report, laptop screen, laptop screen content, and visual details consistent with the DNA references.